  "description": "ATODUK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H112 O22 Sm4,12(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm1A (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2A (Sm) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.795-3.957 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.38-111.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm4(μ-OH)2(dbm)10]·12H2O. Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
